# 📊 Difference Between Map and Struct

| Map                       | Struct                  |
| ------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| Key-Value Pair            | Collection of Fields    |
| Dynamic                   | Fixed Structure         |
| Keys can be added/removed | Fields are predefined   |
| Used for flexible data    | Used for custom objects |

---

# 🎯 Interview Questions

### Q1. What is a Map?

A map is a collection of key-value pairs.

---

### Q2. What is a Struct?

A struct is a user-defined data type that groups multiple fields together.

---

### Q3. Which function is used to remove an element from a map?

```go
delete()
```

---

### Q4. How do you access a struct field?

```go
student.Name
```

---

### Q5. Can a struct contain different data types?

Yes.

Example:

```go
type Student struct {
    Name string
    Age int
    Marks float64
}
```

